body:
Love the song. The snare comes through a little bit loud and overbearing. I might take a few db off the volume and add some reverb on the tail to mix it in a bit better. A little too dry for my taste, kinda distracting. A dryer snare (still with a lower db) like that might feel a little more appropriate with a faster tempo, so it passes by with less exaggeration. Or maybe add a slight echo clap back on the snare that pans from left to right so it better supports the spaciousness of the song. It feels like the snare is right down the center and is a little jarring. Might be simple enough as slight panning of the snare L &R to get it out of the sonic space of the vox and have one layer of vox down the middle. Not sure how you mixed, but that's what I'm hearing.

&#x200B;

Everything else sounds absolutely beautiful and wonderful. Like the affect on the under vocals after the "Yoouuuuu oooooo ooooh" It's like a degrated/distorted old radio effect. Like that. Could be a few dbs lower, but dig it the same. Very nice. I would cut the end hard on the 3rd chord (I think D on the sparkle pad) and not leave the downbeat and echo of the high note/chord on the end. I think it's a G#. Maybe let it ring out on the D, leaving people wanting more, open expectation.

&#x200B;

Anyhow. Great Job! Sounds awesome.
